867 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (Back-to-back fixtures can be challenging when there is limited time between matches. Pixellot systems need time to initialize before a stream can go live, so fixtures cannot be scheduled to overlap. Overlapping events often result in deleted or interrupted streams, which can cause you to miss the end of one match, the start of the next, or both.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
868 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (To minimise this risk, AI Sport Africa recommends the following scheduling convention for back-to-back events:)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
869 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3348 0 R
/E (Schedule the first event of the day to start 5 minutes before the fixture kickoff.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
870 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3349 0 R
/E (Schedule each event to end 15 minutes after the expected end time of the fixture \(or 15 minutes after the scheduled start time of the next fixture\).)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
